<Defs>

  <!--
    The Lantern Wardens (docs/design/peoples-next.md, the first of the eight; docs/design/peoples.md, "Release D";
    Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeoplesD.cs): beast-hunters of the crossroads, who follow the region's great beasts from
    lantern to lantern and keep a book of every creature run down. Medieval, on the game's tribal parent; they arise in
    every age (ariseAges 0~3), and a people of their ways in the industrial or spacer age hunts with guns
    (PeopleKindExtension.ageArms). No uniform: furs, oiled leather and whatever the last hunt paid for, around a hood dyed
    lantern red with its cord (their signature); their towns are palisaded lodges with a trophy hall, kennels and a
    lantern post on every road out (Rimfolk_Plan_WardensLodge). At the gate: a lantern hunt when a pack alpha, a beast
    nemesis or a legend of the region is on the colony's land (Rimfolk_Evt_WardensHunt), their pelt-buyer
    (Rimfolk_Evt_PeltBuyer), and a lantern lit at the colony's gate for one of the colony a beast has taken
    (Rimfolk_Evt_WardensLantern); their lodge asks for the colony's best shots for a drive (Rimfolk_Mission_WardensDrive).
    Their founding (the description): Tobin Garrow, the shepherd who hung his brother's lantern at the crossroads and
    kept it lit eleven years. They raid only when the colony has turned them hostile. Faith (Ideology): people before
    beasts, and the light kept lit (VE Memes' light). Kinds of people: the Venators among them, yttakin, saurids, wood
    elves and the Alpha Genes' animusen, three in four baseliners.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="TribeBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Wardens</defName>
    <label>lantern wardens</label>
    <description>Beast-hunters who follow the region's great beasts from crossroads to crossroads: the alphas that lead packs, the beasts that have taken someone, the old giants the region tells stories about. Where a Warden's lantern burns at a crossroads, someone was taken there, and the Wardens have come to settle it. They keep a book of every creature they have run down, with empty pages for the ones still loose.\n\nTheir ways began with a shepherd called Tobin Garrow, whose village was emptied in one night by something out of the treeline. He hung his dead brother's lantern at the crossroads below the village and swore to keep it lit until the beast was dead, and it took him eleven years. Those who walked with him in the last of them were the first Wardens. Every Warden still carries a soot-blackened lantern at the belt and ties a knot in the red cord on the sleeve for every beast felled.\n\nThey are blunt, patient and short with words, and they talk about beasts the way other people talk about weather. They hunt alongside anyone who asks and buy pelts at the book's rate. Each lodge is kept by its keeper of the book, and the Wardens by their lantern-master.</description>
    <pawnSingular>warden</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>wardens</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>lantern-master</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Medieval</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_Wardens_Warden</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_Wardens</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_WardensTown</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/Wardens</factionIconPath>
    <settlementTexturePath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/WardensTown</settlementTexturePath>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.58, 0.13, 0.09)</li>
      <li>(0.80, 0.26, 0.16)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <hidden>false</hidden>
