        <Yttakin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.04</Yttakin>
        <Neanderthal MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.03</Neanderthal>
        <Hussar MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.02</Hussar>
        <DV_Venator MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,det.venators">0.05</DV_Venator>
        <VRESaurids_Saurid MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,vanillaracesexpanded.saurid">0.02</VRESaurids_Saurid>
        <DevDesigner_XenotypeWoodElves MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,DevDesigner.Elves.Continued">0.02</DevDesigner_XenotypeWoodElves>
        <AG_Animusen MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,sarg.alphagenes">0.02</AG_Animusen>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The Lit Crossroads</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>A beast that takes a person answers for it. People come before beasts, and a Warden puts themselves between the two wherever a lantern is lit; every beast that took someone has a page in the book, and a page is not closed until its ending is written. The light is kept, because the dark is where things wait. Tobin Garrow kept his brother's lantern lit for eleven years, and a Warden who lights one keeps it lit until it is done.</ideoDescription>
    <forcedMemes>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">HumanPrimacy</li>
      <!-- The lantern kept lit at the crossroads: Vanilla Ideology Expanded's light. -->
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">VME_Light</li>
    </forcedMemes>
